{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-032",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 32,
  "title": "Job 32",
  "display_title": "Job 32",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 32,
  "sortOrder": 18032,
  "verseCount": 22,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "So these three men ceased to answer Job, because he was righteous in his own eyes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Then was kindled the wrath of Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite, of the kindred of Ram: against Job was his wrath kindled, because he justified himself rather than God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Also against his three friends was his wrath kindled, because they had found no answer, and yet had condemned Job.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Now Elihu had waited till Job had spoken, because they were elder than he.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "When Elihu saw that there was no answer in the mouth of these three men, then his wrath was kindled.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite answered and said, I am young, and ye are very old; wherefore I was afraid, and durst not shew you mine opinion.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "I said, Days should speak, and multitude of years should teach wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "But there is a spirit in man: and the inspiration of the Almighty giveth them understanding.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Great men are not always wise: neither do the aged understand judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Therefore I said, Hearken to me; I also will shew mine opinion.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Behold, I waited for your words; I gave ear to your reasons, whilst ye searched out what to say.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Yea, I attended unto you, and, behold, there was none of you that convinced Job, or that answered his words:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Lest ye should say, We have found out wisdom: God thrusteth him down, not man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Now he hath not directed his words against me: neither will I answer him with your speeches.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "They were amazed, they answered no more: they left off speaking.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "When I had waited, (for they spake not, but stood still, and answered no more;)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "I said, I will answer also my part, I also will shew mine opinion.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "For I am full of matter, the spirit within me constraineth me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Behold, my belly is as wine which hath no vent; it is ready to burst like new bottles.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "I will speak, that I may be refreshed: I will open my lips and answer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Let me not, I pray you, accept any man’s person, neither let me give flattering titles unto man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:32:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "For I know not to give flattering titles; in so doing my maker would soon take me away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 32:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:32:22"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
